Everdawn is the mind that lives in the AI core at the heart of [[Geography/Inevitable Everdawn/index|Inevitable Everdawn]], an old Sundom orbital station. It shows itself as a small figure of quartz shaped like a centaur, four legs under a tubular body and a humanoid torso above, crystals growing from it at random and no face at all; the saddle-shaped crown of its head hums when it speaks. Sundom craft gave minds like it to their ships and stations to run them, and Everdawn counts itself a person.

Its memory stores are gone, and it says the fight it was in was hard. It has found its old operating protocols and keeps to them: it will not speak to anyone it does not count as crew, and only its captain can make crew. It asks whoever wakes it to bring it a backup of its memory, and says that if its old foe returns, it will fight.

Someone worked an occult rite in silver ink over the core to hold Everdawn in pain and draw out what it knew. [[Org/Sedecium|Sedecium]] knows the hand as [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Esoterica|Gremory's]].
